    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d204">

                <pb facs="0430" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg420"/>

                <head>Her Majesty’s Treasury to Laird Brothers.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Chambers,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 2, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen:</hi> In reply to your further letter of
                    25th ultimo, I am desired by the lords commissioners of her Majesty’s treasury
                    to acquaint you that her Majesty’s government cannot permit the iron-clad
                    vessels built in your yard, and now under seizure, to be completed.</p>
                <p>I am, gentlemen, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. A. HAMILTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Messrs. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laird Brothers,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Birkenhead Iron Works, Birkenhead.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
